{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicSymCoeff_eq_neg_five_twelfths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicSymCoeff_eq_neg_five_twelfths","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L279-L286","doc":"The two inter-cusp cross-terms ($2 \\times (-1/4) = -1/2$) flip the sign and quintuple the\nmagnitude of the cubic longitude coefficient on the symmetric 3-cusp locus:\n$a_{3,\\mathrm{sym}} = -\\frac{5}{12} = -5\\,a_{3,\\mathrm{self}}$, with $a_{3,\\mathrm{self}} > 0$\nand $a_{3,\\mathrm{sym}} < 0$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicLon_sym_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicLon_sym_locus","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L272-L277","doc":"On the symmetric 3-cusp deformation $(u, u, u)$, the cubic longitude jet equals\n$a_{3,\\mathrm{sym}}\\,u^3 = -\\frac{5}{12} u^3$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicLon_single_cusp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicLon_single_cusp","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L266-L270","doc":"On a single-cusp deformation $(u, 0, 0)$, the cubic longitude jet equals $+\\frac{1}{12} u^3$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.a3SymCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.a3SymCoeff","kind":"def","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L262-L264","doc":"Effective cubic longitude coefficient on the symmetric 3-cusp locus $u_1 = u_2 = u_3 = u$:\n$a_{3,\\mathrm{sym}} = a_{3,\\mathrm{self}} + 2\\,a_{3,\\mathrm{cross}}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicLonJet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanCubicLonJet","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L257-L260","doc":"The cubic jet of $\\mathrm{Im}(v_1(u_1, u_2, u_3))$ around $u = (0,0,0)$:\n$v_1^{(3)}(u_1, u_2, u_3) = a_{3,\\mathrm{self}}\\,u_1^3 + a_{3,\\mathrm{cross}}\\,u_1(u_2^2 + u_3^2)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.a3CrossCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.a3CrossCoeff","kind":"def","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L253-L255","doc":"The exact 3rd-order imaginary Taylor coefficient of $v_i$ for inter-cusp coupling $u_i u_j^2$ ($j \\neq i$):\n$\\frac{1}{2!} \\mathrm{Im}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\partial^3 v_i}{\\partial u_i \\partial u_j^2}\\big|_{u=0}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = -\\frac{1}{4}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.a3SelfCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.a3SelfCoeff","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L249-L251","doc":"The exact 3rd-order imaginary Taylor coefficient of $v_i$ for self-deformation $u_i^3$:\n$\\frac{1}{3!} \\mathrm{Im}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\partial^3 v_i}{\\partial u_i^3}\\big|_{u=0}\\right) = \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{12}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.kappaBorSym_nz_frame_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.kappaBorSym_nz_frame_neg","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L240-L245","doc":"In the NZ per-cusp frame where $\\kappa_{\\mathrm{diag}} = -1$ and $\\kappa_{\\mathrm{off}} = 0$,\n$\\kappa_{\\mathrm{Bor}}^{\\mathrm{sym}} = -3 < 0$ (preserving the per-cusp sign). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.kappaBorSym_of_zero_offDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.kappaBorSym_of_zero_offDiag","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L231-L238","doc":"Because the Borromean 3-cusp NZ Jacobian is strictly diagonal (`scaledLonJac_offDiag_zero`),\nthe quadratic inter-cusp coupling vanishes ($\\kappa_{\\mathrm{off}} = 0$), forcing\n$\\kappa_{\\mathrm{Bor}}^{\\mathrm{sym}} = 3\\,\\kappa_{\\mathrm{diag}}$. In particular, inter-cusp\nquadratic cross-terms cannot flip the sign of $\\kappa_{\\mathrm{Bor}}^{\\mathrm{sym}}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanQuadForm_sym_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanQuadForm_sym_locus","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L224-L229","doc":"Evaluating the 3-cusp quadratic form on the symmetric deformation locus $u_1 = u_2 = u_3 = u$\nyields $\\kappa_{\\mathrm{Bor}}^{\\mathrm{sym}} \\cdot u^2$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.kappaBorSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.kappaBorSym","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L219-L222","doc":"Symmetric-locus ($u_1 = u_2 = u_3 = u$) effective quadratic curvature coefficient\n$\\kappa_{\\mathrm{Bor}}^{\\mathrm{sym}} = 3\\,\\kappa_{\\mathrm{diag}} + 6\\,\\kappa_{\\mathrm{off}}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanQuadForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.borromeanQuadForm","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L214-L217","doc":"General $S_3$-symmetric 3-cusp quadratic curvature form with diagonal per-cusp curvature\n$\\kappa_{\\mathrm{diag}}$ and off-diagonal inter-cusp coupling $\\kappa_{\\mathrm{off}}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJac_offDiag_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJac_offDiag_zero","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L204-L210","doc":"All 6 off-diagonal entries ($i \\neq j$) of the $3 \\times 3$ Borromean longitude Jacobian\nvanish identically in both real and imaginary parts, proving that the shared octahedral\ntetrahedra produce zero quadratic inter-cusp coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJac_im_eq_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJac_im_eq_diag","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L197-L202","doc":"The imaginary part of the scaled $3 \\times 3$ longitude Jacobian $4\\,J^{(1)}$ is strictly\ndiagonal: $4\\,\\mathrm{Im}(J^{(1)}_{ij}) = -8\\,\\delta_{ij}$, so $J^{(1)}_{ij} = -2i\\,\\delta_{ij}$\n(and the cusp modulus matrix $\\tau_{ij} = -J^{(1)}_{ij} = +2i\\,\\delta_{ij}$). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJac_re_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJac_re_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L191-L195","doc":"The real part of the scaled $3 \\times 3$ longitude Jacobian $4\\,J^{(1)}$ vanishes identically\nfor all $i, j \\in \\{0, 1, 2\\}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJacIm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJacIm","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L186-L189","doc":"Imaginary part of the scaled $3 \\times 3$ longitude Jacobian\n$4\\,J^{(1)} = C_{\\mathrm{lon}} \\cdot S^{(1)}$ in $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJacRe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledLonJacRe","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L181-L184","doc":"Real part of the scaled $3 \\times 3$ longitude Jacobian\n$4\\,J^{(1)} = C_{\\mathrm{lon}} \\cdot S^{(1)}$ in $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSys_mul_scaledZ1_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSys_mul_scaledZ1_im","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L173-L177","doc":"Exact verification that the imaginary part of $M_{\\mathrm{sys}} \\cdot S^{(1)}$ vanishes\nidentically across all $8 \\times 3$ entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSys_mul_scaledZ1_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSys_mul_scaledZ1_re","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L165-L171","doc":"Exact verification that $S^{(1)} = 4\\,\\frac{\\partial Z}{\\partial u}\\big|_{u=0}$ solves the\nlinearized gluing system $M_{\\mathrm{sys}} \\cdot S^{(1)} = 4 \\begin{pmatrix} 0_{5 \\times 3} \\\\ I_3 \\end{pmatrix}$:\nthe real part equals $4$ on the meridian diagonal $r = 5 + j$ and $0$ everywhere else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysMulScaledZ1Im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysMulScaledZ1Im","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L161-L163","doc":"Imaginary part of the $8 \\times 3$ product $M_{\\mathrm{sys}} \\cdot S^{(1)}$ in $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysMulScaledZ1Re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysMulScaledZ1Re","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L157-L159","doc":"Real part of the $8 \\times 3$ product $M_{\\mathrm{sys}} \\cdot S^{(1)}$ in $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledZ1_normSq_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledZ1_normSq_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L150-L155","doc":"Every entry of the scaled $8 \\times 3$ shape Jacobian $4\\,\\frac{\\partial Z_k}{\\partial u_j}\\big|_{u=0}$\nhas Gaussian norm-squared $(\\mathrm{Re})^2 + (\\mathrm{Im})^2 = 2$; in particular all 24 entries\nare non-zero, demonstrating that every ideal tetrahedron responds to all 3 cusps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledZ1Im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledZ1Im","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L138-L148","doc":"Imaginary part of the scaled $8 \\times 3$ shape sensitivity matrix\n$S^{(1)} = 4\\,\\frac{\\partial Z}{\\partial u}\\big|_{u=0}$ over $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledZ1Re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.scaledZ1Re","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L126-L136","doc":"Real part of the scaled $8 \\times 3$ shape sensitivity matrix\n$S^{(1)} = 4\\,\\frac{\\partial Z}{\\partial u}\\big|_{u=0}$ over $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.cLonIm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.cLonIm","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L121-L122","doc":"Imaginary part of the $3 \\times 8$ linearized longitude operator $C_{\\mathrm{lon}}$ over $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.cLonRe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.cLonRe","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L117-L119","doc":"Real part of the $3 \\times 8$ linearized longitude operator\n$C_{\\mathrm{lon}} = A_{\\mathrm{lon}} + U_{\\mathrm{lon}}\\,\\mathrm{diag}(w^{(0)})$ over $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysIm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysIm","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L114-L115","doc":"Imaginary part of the $8 \\times 8$ linearized gluing operator $M_{\\mathrm{sys}}$ over $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysRe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.mSysRe","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L110-L112","doc":"Real part of the $8 \\times 8$ linearized gluing operator\n$M_{\\mathrm{sys}} = A_{\\mathrm{sys}} + U_{\\mathrm{sys}}\\,\\mathrm{diag}(w^{(0)})$ over $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lonU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lonU","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L103-L108","doc":"Integer $\\log(1/(1-z_k))$ coefficients $U_{\\mathrm{lon}} = -B_{\\mathrm{lon}}$ for the 3\nlongitude rows of `L6a4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lonA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lonA","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L97-L101","doc":"Integer $\\log(z_k)$ coefficients $A_{\\mathrm{lon}}$ for the 3 longitude rows of `L6a4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.sysU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.sysU","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L85-L95","doc":"Integer $\\log(1/(1-z_k))$ coefficients $U_{\\mathrm{sys}} = -B_{\\mathrm{sys}}$ for the $8 \\times 8$\nsystem formed by the 5 independent edge rows $(0,1,2,3,4)$ and the 3 meridian rows of `L6a4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.sysA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.sysA","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L73-L83","doc":"Integer $\\log(z_k)$ coefficients $A_{\\mathrm{sys}}$ for the $8 \\times 8$ system formed by\nthe 5 independent edge rows $(0,1,2,3,4)$ and the 3 meridian rows of SnapPy's `L6a4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.w0Im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.w0Im","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L69-L71","doc":"Imaginary part of $w_k^{(0)} = z_k^{(0)} / (1 - z_k^{(0)}) \\in \\mathbb{Z}[i]$ at the complete\nregular-octahedral structure of `L6a4`: $+1$ on all 8 tetrahedra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.w0Re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.w0Re","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BorromeanThreeCuspNZHessian.lean#L65-L67","doc":"Real part of $w_k^{(0)} = z_k^{(0)} / (1 - z_k^{(0)}) \\in \\mathbb{Z}[i]$ at the complete\nregular-octahedral structure of `L6a4`: $0$ on tetrahedra $\\{0,5,6,7\\}$ and $-1$ on $\\{1,2,3,4\\}$. ","signatureChunk":0}]}